WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.193
- Mole sauce is a very
special Mexican dish.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.413
It's really the go-to plate
for any major celebration.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.200
Our mole sauce started
from just a family recipe;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.200
but now, we are making about
2,000 pounds of mole a day.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.950
We never thought in our wildest dreams

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.859
that that was going to happen.

00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:28.276
(emotional violin music)

00:00:29.941 --> 00:00:32.460
(playful piano music)

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.550
There are nearly one million

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.110
Mexicans living in the tri-state area.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:40.530
Half of them are from
Puebla, where we are from,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:44.003
and they still want the
flavor from back home.

00:00:44.003 --> 00:00:46.280
(Damiana speaking Spanish)

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.730
That's what we eat, she said.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.640
My family has been producing
mole at Mole Poblano

00:00:54.077 --> 00:00:55.990
La Asuncion for several years now.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:01:00.060
The business is run by three
generations, all of them women:

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.643
my grandmother, my mother and me.

00:01:04.848 --> 00:01:06.880
(uplifting violin music)

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.880
Mole just means a sauce
with a lot of ingredients:

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.800
chilies and spices

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.790
and sugar and chocolate.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:22.763
We also use almonds,
raisins and sesame seeds.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:28.670
We toast all of those ingredients up

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.513
and also have to grind them as well.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.000
That's when we put the pot up,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.970
and then we start heating the oil

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:40.833
with some garlic and with some onions.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.090
And when the onions and garlic are done,

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.310
that's when start pouring in our chilies,

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:51.263
and that's when we start
putting the ingredients.

00:01:55.910 --> 00:02:00.910
You have to have very strong
arms to keep stirring that mole

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.450
until everything is completely
integrated into the sauce,

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:07.710
until everything looks dark.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.613
Our recipe, it takes about two days.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:18.100
It has to go through
Grandma to get approved.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.017
(speaking Spanish)

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:25.520
My grandmother moved to New
York from Piaxtla, Puebla

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.650
in the 1970s because she had children

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.363
and mouths to feed back home.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.368
(speaking Spanish)

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:57.290
And then word of mouth started increasing.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:59.950
Now, the mole sauce is
being distributed in bodegas

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.250
and Mexican stores and
restaurants here in New York

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:08.810
and in the tri-state area, and
also all around the country.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:12.910
The longing for a little
something of where you come from

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:17.570
I think played in our success
here in New York City.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:20.283
It's authentic as it can possibly be.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.390
The most important part of our day

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.440
is at 2 o'clock in the afternoon

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.370
when we have lunch together as a family.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.910
I guess it's a very big expression

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:35.460
of how much we love our
job, we love our mole,

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:38.310
and we love each other in the family.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:42.217
I guess that transfers also in
the mole sauce that we make.

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:52.792
(electronic chiming)

